# Pinned platform descriptor source for the pocketforge-sim image (reproducibility anchor).
# platform is PUBLIC (made public 2026-06-27, tsp-qc1.4), so the Dockerfile clones it directly at
# the pinned commit below — truly reproducible-from-clean, no out-of-band input.
repo   = https://github.com/pocketforge-os/platform.git
commit = a86adf6fa4c5d8f4a97db50d0fa23035adfe816a
ref    = origin/main
# Descriptor SHA-256 at this commit (platform main @ PR #309, tsp-h5ed.46.28 — the bump past pfvd's
# platform.pin 24ace826; the prior pin 6cc66646 (PR #81) is a linear ancestor). The a133/a523
# descriptors change: a133 sticks are unsigned 12-bit (0..4095, flat/fuzz 0), a133 west/north use
# the canonical positional codes (BTN_NORTH 307), both gain VOL-/VOL+ system rows (KEY_VOLUMEDOWN/
# KEY_VOLUMEUP), plus the v2 [model]/[physical] rows the sim does not read. So the
# `uinput_synth.py plan` output CHANGES for both devices (old: a133 22c33607…, a523 65143215…) and
# now equals pfvd's vendored plan fixtures byte for byte (a133 3a210461…, a523 955015bb…), the same
# plans platform 24ace826 yields:
#   devices/a133/capabilities.toml 2b77f51f7c350efd3e90f5c815bff8634637b8dcd8d4c37819de5321a3c4a1a7
#   devices/a523/capabilities.toml 44a095d7974ec206aba37774c99ad4ad975f737d189218458327e909bc8daeb3
